ID=NC000054
BIB_ID=BC000005
TITLE=Satire in the Atomic Era - "A bit terrifying"
LOCATOR=Los Angeles Examiner, 11/14/1959
USE=Contemporary Reception
TEXT=In a discussion of Lehrer's particular brand of satire ("While he makes you laugh you are also made aware of some of the ridiculous antics of modern man"), the Los Angeles Examiner writer wrote "He made a great deal of man's 'golden dream' of blowing himself off the planet. This is an awesome thought. To hear reverberant laughter on such a macabre subject is a bit terrifying."
---
ID=NC000055
BIB_ID=BC000006
TITLE=WWAGTWWG in the 'Age of anxiety'
LOCATOR=The Peninsula Times Tribune, 10/27/1958
USE=Contemporary Reception
TEXT=Dorothy Nichols, in reviewing Lehrer's sold-out performance Oct. 25, 1958 at Stanford's Memorial Hall, wrote that "Like the best satirists he is a gloomy idealist, measuring professions of faith against performances." This included WWAGTWWG, which Nichols said Lehrer "[put] the age of anxiety" into.
---
